 "result": "I made three fixes:\n\n- **Merged c2–c4 into one condition** (\"on Aurora's still-unstarted milestone due September 30\"), so the relation, status, and date facts all live under a single condition. Now `i-decoy-rel` (no milestone at all) fails only that one condition instead of three separate ones.\n- **Reworded the request** from \"milestone that's due September 30 and hasn't started yet\" to \"still-unstarted milestone due September 30\" — \"still-unstarted\" is now an adjective directly on \"milestone,\" removing the reading where \"hasn't started yet\" could describe the issue's own workflow state.\n- **Set every seeded issue's workflow state to \"In Progress\"** (none are \"Todo\"), so no issue could be mistaken as \"not started\" under an issue-status misreading — closing the loophole that made `i-decoy-status` arguably compliant.",
